  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "What is the $x$ -coordinate of the point on the curve $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}(7 x-6),$ where the tangent is parallel to $\\mathrm{x}$ -axis?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "oLz6E",
      "text": "$-\\frac{1}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "eZ9tb",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{7}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bNQNF",
      "text": "$\\frac{6}{7}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "AtU8c",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$f(x)=\\sqrt{x}(7 x-6)=7 x^{3 / 2}-6 x^{1 / 2}$\r\n\r\n$f^{\\prime}(x)=7 \\times \\frac{3}{2} x^{1 / 2}-6 \\times \\frac{1}{2} x^{-1 / 2}$\r\n\r\nWhen tangent is parallel to $x$ axis $f^{\\prime}(x)=0$\r\n\r\nor, $\\quad \\frac{21}{2} \\mathrm{x}^{1 / 2}-3 \\mathrm{x}^{-1 / 2}=0$\r\n\r\n$\\frac{21}{2} \\sqrt{x}=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{x}}$\r\n\r\nor, $7 x=2 \\Rightarrow x=\\frac{2}{7}$",
    "image": null
  },
